{"name":"Double Jeopardy","hex":"#4d786c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Double Jeopardy","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A round of questioning or other situation where the possible gains and/or losses from choices are magnified."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Double_Jeopardy"}],"entries":[{"title":"Double Jeopardy (1955 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Double Jeopardy is an American crime film directed by R. G. Springsteen and starring Rod Cameron, Gale Robbins and Allison Hayes. It is also known by the alternative title of Crooked Ring."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/59/Double_Jeopardy_%281955_film%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Double_Jeopardy_(1955_film)"},{"title":"Double Jeopardy (1992 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Double Jeopardy is a 1992 television thriller film directed by Lawrence Schiller and starring Rachel Ward, Bruce Boxleitner, Sela Ward and Sally Kirkland."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/ab/Double_Jeopardy_%281992_film%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Double_Jeopardy_(1992_film)"},{"title":"Double jeopardy","blocks":[{"text":"In jurisprudence, double jeopardy is a procedural defence that prevents an accused person from being tried again on the same or similar charges following an acquittal or conviction. Double jeopardy is a common concept in criminal law – in civil law, a similar concept is that of res judicata."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Double_jeopardy"},{"title":"Jeopardy!","blocks":[{"text":"Jeopardy! is an American television game show created by Merv Griffin. The show is a quiz competition that reverses the traditional question-and-answer format of many quiz shows. Rather than being given questions, contestants are instead given general knowledge clues in 